{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-bm25-human", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "1-1_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To help you, I would suggest that you try to eat smaller, more frequent meals throughout the day to reduce symptoms of acid reflux. You can also try incorporating high-fiber foods like oatmeal, brown rice, and sweet potatoes into your diet, as they can help keep your meals small and reduce symptoms. Additionally, you may want to consider avoiding trigger foods like citrus fruits, spicy foods, and fatty or rich foods that can exacerbate acid reflux. Drinking water can also help by diluting stomach acid and relieving symptoms. Chewing gum can also help increase saliva production and reduce acid in the esophagus. It's also a good idea to elevate the head of your bed by 6-8 inches to reduce acid reflux at night. Finally, consider losing weight if you're overweight, as excess weight can put pressure on the stomach and worsen acid reflux symptoms. Consult with your doctor or a registered dietitian for personalized advice.  Document ID: Doc1, Doc2, Doc", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0023-72-04650:5": 5.121960163116455, "clueweb22-en0032-81-17497:10": 5.015613555908203, "clueweb22-en0000-61-09646:7": 4.920449256896973, "clueweb22-en0033-70-16648:0": 4.801593780517578, "clueweb22-en0041-54-03695:8": 4.665760040283203}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I want to stop doom scrolling.", "I'm thinking of internet detoxing.", "I spend too much time on my phone.", "I want to change my lifestyle."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0023-72-04650:5": 5.121960163116455, "clueweb22-en0032-81-17497:10": 5.015613555908203, "clueweb22-en0000-61-09646:7": 4.920449256896973, "clueweb22-en0033-70-16648:0": 4.801593780517578, "clueweb22-en0041-54-03695:8": 4.665760040283203, "clueweb22-en0028-76-08961:2": 4.584737777709961, "clueweb22-en0006-37-07600:10": 4.429483413696289, "clueweb22-en0020-51-04974:3": 4.391687393188477, "clueweb22-en0009-73-15619:9": 4.141872