{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-bm25-human", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "3-1_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The H-taping method is a more effective way to tape your finger, especially for injured pulleys. It involves cutting a length of rigid athletic tape, cutting it in half lengthwise, and then placing it on the injured finger with the bridge on the inside of the finger, sitting on the crease of the joint on the upper end of the injured pulley. You then flex your finger 60\u00b0 at the joint being taped, wrap the upper bit of the tape in a ring, and then wrap the other ring of tape below the joint. This method is more effective than other taping methods in keeping tendons close to the bone and supporting the job of injured finger pulleys while flexed and under pressure. It's also been shown to increase the crimping strength of injured fingers by an average of 13%.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:12": 6.55859899520874, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:9": 4.965534687042236, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:7": 4.537324905395508, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 4.35611629486084, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:2": 4.279062271118164}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:12": 6.55859899520874, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:9": 4.965534687042236, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:7": 4.537324905395508, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 4.35611629486084, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:2": 4.279062271118164, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:10": 3.8076488971710205, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:10": 3.5307397842407227, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:11": 3.5307204723358154, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:8": 3.2048048973083496, "clueweb22-en0041-91-12714:5": 2.7658910751342773, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:8": 2.5032310485839844, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:9": 2.373595952987671, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:14": 2.2980947494506836, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:1": 2.1215765476226807, "clueweb22-en0041-91-12714:6": 2.055565595626831, "clueweb22