{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-bm25-human", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "No, it doesn't mean you will run out of milk for your baby. It means that alcohol may affect the release of oxytocin, which can affect the let-down of breast milk. This can lead to lower breast milk volumes. However, it's not a guarantee that you will run out of milk. You can still produce milk, but it might be affected by the alcohol. It's always best to talk to your healthcare provider for personalized advice on breastfeeding and alcohol. They can help you understand how alcohol may affect your milk supply and provide guidance on how to manage it. Additionally, if you do choose to drink alcohol, you can express and store your milk beforehand to ensure your baby continues to receive the milk they need. This way, you can enjoy a drink while still providing for your baby's needs.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0042-99-06708:13": 6.252080917358398, "clueweb22-en0005-68-03159:8": 6.229964733123779, "clueweb22-en0042-99-06708:12": 6.11025333404541, "clueweb22-en0038-72-00255:5": 6.040826797485352, "clueweb22-en0038-72-00255:4": 6.019284725189209}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am interested in low-carb food."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0042-99-06708:13": 6.252080917358398, "clueweb22-en0005-68-03159:8": 6.229964733123779, "clueweb22-en0042-99-06708:12": 6.11025333404541, "clueweb22-en0038-72-00255:5": 6.040826797485352, "clueweb22-en0038-72-00255:4": 6.019284725189209, "clueweb22-en0036-86-10058:4": 6.010019302368164, "clueweb22-en0041-35-06877:13": 5.975403785705566, "clueweb22-en0044-37-08521:7": 5.939815998077393, "clueweb22-en0046-33-11913:7": 5.937195301055908, "clueweb22-en0044-37-08521:4": 5.889166831970215, "clueweb22-en0044-37-08521:3": 5.805749893188477, "clueweb22-en0014-46-02684:5": 5.755528450012207, "clueweb22-en0029-93-12021:21": 5.714447975158691, "clueweb22-en0031-57-16983:1": 5.647042751312256, "clueweb22-en00