{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-bm25-human", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_4", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "CO2 laser treatment works by emitting a specific wavelength of light that targets water molecules in the skin, vaporizing skin cells and making way for fresh, clear new skin. It also penetrates the skin's deeper dermis layer to stimulate new collagen production, which firms and smooths skin over time. This can help address fine lines and wrinkles, discoloration, acne scars, stretch marks, and uneven skin texture. The treatment can be done on the full face or as a spot treatment for isolated concerns. However, it's an aggressive laser and should be used cautiously in all skin types, and it's not typically recommended for people with darker skin tones due to the increased risk of hyperpigmentation. The UltraPulse laser is a popular type of CO2 laser.  It's an outpatient procedure that can take anywhere from 30 minutes to two hours, depending on the size of the treatment area and aggressiveness of treatment. You may be numbed with local anesthesia or put under general anesthesia", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:1": 10.468457221984863, "clueweb22-en0032-14-04213:8": 8.16459846496582, "clueweb22-en0031-65-04139:2": 8.018044471740723, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:13": 7.90927267074585, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:2": 7.685881614685059}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I've noticed dark spots and uneven tone on my face.", "I have visible pores on my cheeks and nose.", "I usually wear makeup to even out my complexion.", "I am a 40-year-old woman.", "I'm interested in treatments that improve my skin with minimal downtime."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:1": 10.468457221984863, "clueweb22-en0032-14-04213:8": 8.16459846496582, "clueweb22-en0031-65-04139:2": 8.018044471740723, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:13": 7.90927267074585, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:2": 7.685881614685059, "clueweb22-en0018-50-01341:4": 7.6539793014526