{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-bm25-human", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Fractional CO2 lasers deliver a partial beam of light that targets only a fraction of the skin, in a pixelated pattern. This means that they remove less skin compared to the other type, which is fully ablative. Fully ablative CO2 lasers completely ablate the treatment area, stripping away all superficial skin hit with the laser beam and heating up the deeper dermal layer to trigger a regenerative healing response. This type of laser is more aggressive and requires general anesthesia, with a minimum of two weeks of downtime. Fractional lasers, on the other hand, are less aggressive and can be adjusted to suit your skin concerns, with only some skin removed and a shorter recovery time of a few days. They are also more suitable for a range of skin types and tones. Choose the one that best fits your needs and preferences. If you want a more intense treatment with longer-lasting results, fully ablative might be the better option. If you prefer a less invasive procedure with minimal downtime, fractional", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:10": 7.152713298797607, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:9": 6.157963275909424, "clueweb22-en0031-16-03068:4": 5.3217973709106445, "clueweb22-en0025-73-01656:10": 4.519365310668945, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:12": 4.239719390869141}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I've noticed dark spots and uneven tone on my face.", "I have visible pores on my cheeks and nose.", "I usually wear makeup to even out my complexion.", "I'm interested in treatments that improve my skin with minimal downtime."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:10": 7.152713298797607, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:9": 6.157963275909424, "clueweb22-en0031-16-03068:4": 5.3217973709106445, "clueweb22-en0025-73-01656:10": 4.519365310668945, "clueweb22-en0004-01-09924:12": 4.239719390869141, "clueweb22-en0031-16-03068:7": 4.215891361236