{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-bm25-human", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "6-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Possible side effects of microdermabrasion include bruising, redness, swelling, tenderness or even petechiae (dark-colored spots indicative of bleeding under the skin). You may also experience mild inflammation after a microdermabrasion treatment, which will likely disappear in a few hours. As for chemical peels, common side effects include redness, swelling and flaking. The skin will be sensitive to sunlight for several days or weeks until it has completely healed. In the case of deeper peels, the side effects can be severe and carry a risk of infection and scarring. Peels performed on darker skin tones carry a risk of skin discoloration and demarcation between treated and untreated skin.  Additionally, there is a risk that microdermabrasion can spread infections from one part of your skin to another. So you should not have microdermabrasion if you have skin infections such as impetigo, or have had warts, herpes and other", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0000-24-11991:11": 4.735245227813721, "clueweb22-en0033-06-10590:10": 4.394129276275635, "clueweb22-en0036-14-13056:11": 4.24993896484375, "clueweb22-en0032-47-03490:7": 4.18820858001709, "clueweb22-en0037-85-14845:4": 3.682992935180664}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I've noticed dark spots and uneven tone on my face.", "I have visible pores on my cheeks and nose.", "I usually wear makeup to even out my complexion.", "I am a 40-year-old woman.", "I'm interested in treatments that improve my skin with minimal downtime."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0000-24-11991:11": 4.735245227813721, "clueweb22-en0033-06-10590:10": 4.394129276275635, "clueweb22-en0036-14-13056:11": 4.24993896484375, "clueweb22-en0032-47-03490:7": 4.18820858001709, "clueweb22-en0037-85-14845:4": 3.682992935180664, "clueweb22-en0012-02-13520:11": 3.5674357414245605, "clueweb22-en0000-24-11991:12": 3.458346366882