{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-bm25-human", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_6", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "You can try the \"Time Boxing\" technique, which is similar to the Pomodoro Technique but allows for more flexibility. Instead of setting a timer for a fixed amount of time, you allocate a specific block of time for a task, say 90 minutes. During this time, you focus exclusively on that task without any interruptions. When the time is up, you take a break. This way, you can work in longer blocks of time and still have breaks in between. Alternatively, you can try the \"2-minute rule\", where you commit to working on a task for just 2 minutes without any distractions. Often, getting started is the hardest part, and you'll find that you can continue working beyond the initial 2 minutes. This approach can help you build momentum and make progress on tasks without feeling too restricted by a timer. Would you like to explore more strategies or discuss how to implement these techniques in your daily work?", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0000-09-08980:8": 4.674491882324219, "clueweb22-en0022-63-14535:8": 3.5577049255371094, "clueweb22-en0038-55-03763:3": 3.370903253555298, "clueweb22-en0000-09-08980:10": 3.2746245861053467, "clueweb22-en0006-85-12176:10": 3.2180190086364746}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I work in an office.", "I have a sedentary lifestyle."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0000-09-08980:8": 4.674491882324219, "clueweb22-en0022-63-14535:8": 3.5577049255371094, "clueweb22-en0038-55-03763:3": 3.370903253555298, "clueweb22-en0000-09-08980:10": 3.2746245861053467, "clueweb22-en0006-85-12176:10": 3.2180190086364746, "clueweb22-en0006-78-14996:6": 2.897371530532837, "clueweb22-en0022-63-14535:7": 2.8855345249176025, "clueweb22-en0036-62-06149:12": 2.853356122970581, "clueweb22-en0006-90-16096:9": 2.7471773624420166, "clueweb22-en0022-63-14535:9": 2.709611415863037, "clueweb22-en0027-17-19946:9": 2.708122730255127, "clueweb22-en