{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-bm25-human", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-2_5", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "The jockey is a small wheel located on the front of a trailer or caravan, used for low-speed maneuvering or manual steering when the trailer is decoupled from the towing vehicle. It's also known as a guide wheel, and it's used to move, retain, locate, and add tension to a chain, rope, or cable. In the context of your bike, the jockey wheels are part of the derailleur system, and they help to take up slack in the bike chain as it's fed from one of the front chainrings. They're held in a cage and are used to guide the chain through the gears. I hope that helps! Let me know if you have any other questions.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0032-78-01787:0": 1.494575023651123, "clueweb22-en0032-78-01787:1": 0.162258118391037, "clueweb22-en0028-52-17752:16": 0.07249133288860321, "clueweb22-en0028-52-17752:17": -0.5982720255851746, "clueweb22-en0019-18-17131:9": -1.2121264934539795}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I'm a casual bike rider.", "I take my bike in the train and the bus.", "I like biking even in rainy weather and in the forest."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0032-78-01787:0": 1.494575023651123, "clueweb22-en0032-78-01787:1": 0.162258118391037, "clueweb22-en0028-52-17752:16": 0.07249133288860321, "clueweb22-en0028-52-17752:17": -0.5982720255851746, "clueweb22-en0019-18-17131:9": -1.2121264934539795, "clueweb22-en0035-43-13674:3": -1.5521981716156006, "clueweb22-en0041-55-13857:2": -2.1185224056243896, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:3": -2.2350895404815674, "clueweb22-en0014-43-14118:1": -2.294764280319214, "clueweb22-en0040-35-09091:5": -2.5607409477233887, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:1": -2.5654687881469727, "clueweb22-en0019-78-08540:14": -2.5886054039001465, "clueweb22-en0039-65-07416:0": -2.6520867347717285, "clueweb22-en0004-74-03600:1": -2.7126569747924805, "clueweb22-en0035-43-13674:2": -2.7757859230041504, "clueweb22-en0005-6